# --- OS / editor noise -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Publisher PDFs (copyright) ----------------------------------------------
# Every paper and SI this corpus is built from stays local. curation/SOURCES.md
# records the DOI and the exact filename for each one, so anyone can fetch their
# own copy and re-run the curation scripts against it.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx

# --- Derived page renders ----------------------------------------------------
# 00_pages/ is produced from the local PDF by each curation's page-render step.
# ~110 MB of PNG that regenerates in seconds; keeping it would make the clone
# larger than the data it supports.
curation/*/00_pages/

# --- Vendored upstream clones ------------------------------------------------
# Untrusted third-party repos cloned for comparison (FALCON, LipidAI). They
# carry their own .git, which cannot be nested here, and they are not ours to
# redistribute. The curation PROVENANCE.md in each folder records the URL and
# the commit that was read.
curation/*/repo/

# --- Superseded dataset snapshots --------------------------------------------
# provenance/superseded/ holds ~107 MB of pre-rebuild snapshots and timestamped
# backups. The one file with real provenance value -- the pristine upstream
# LNPDB download -- is force-added and tracked; the rest are reproducible by
# checking out an earlier commit.
provenance/superseded/*
!provenance/superseded/LNPDB_official_download_20261028.csv

# --- Regenerable caches ------------------------------------------------------
cache/
*.bak_*

# --- Playwright MCP scratch (snapshots/console logs written to the cwd) ------
# The MCP server drops these into whatever directory it is launched from, which
# is the repo root. They are session artifacts, never inputs to anything.
.playwright-mcp/

# --- Publisher source ASSETS, not just PDFs (copyright) ----------------------
# The *.pdf rule above was added for copyright. The same reasoning covers every
# other asset a publisher serves: figure rasters, supplementary archives, JATS
# XML, TIFFs. Measured 2026-11-10 while preparing a push: a plain `git add -A`
# would have added **60.2 MB in 101 files** from `curation/*/source/` --
# 53 jpg, 16 xml, 14 png, 7 jpeg, 4 tif, 3 zip -- to a repo that is **PUBLIC**.
# Several of those papers are subscription-only or CC BY-NC-ND, where ND alone
# forbids redistribution. Publishing them would be republication, not fair use,
# and CLAUDE.md §8 requires CC0/CC-BY compatibility before any corpus release.
#
# What we DO track is our own derived work: the extraction scripts, the measured
# values, the QC JSONs and the decision logs. Those are ours and they are what a
# cloud session needs. A curation that must re-read a figure re-acquires it with
# provenance/tools/ (pmc_fetch.py, fetch_paper.py) -- see BROWSER_ACQUISITION.md
# for which publishers need a browser and therefore cannot be re-acquired
# headlessly.
curation/*/source/
curation/*/source_epmc/
curation/*/00_pages/
curation/*/renders/
curation/*/figs/
# `source_epmc/` is the Europe PMC fetch directory -- a `source/` rule does not
# cover it, and it held 6 publisher JPEGs. Name every acquisition directory.

# Page RENDERS and annotated OVERLAYS are reproductions of the publisher's page
# or figure, so they carry the same restriction as the asset they came from --
# an overlay is the figure plus our annotation, not a new work. Each is
# regenerable from the local source by that curation's own render step, so
# nothing is lost by excluding them. (Measured: 37.7 MB staged before this rule,
# led by 1.8 MB / 1.7 MB SI page renders.)
# A pattern containing ** did NOT match here; a SLASHLESS pattern matches at
# any depth, which is why the *.pdf rule above has always worked. Use that form.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tif
*.tiff

# Slashless so they match at any depth, exactly like the *.pdf rule above.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tif
*.tiff
curation/*/source_epmc/
curation/*/renders/
curation/*/figs/
